<Defs>
  <!--
  RM_Dustveil: owned RM_ port of the Alpha Animals AngelMoth (sarg.alphaanimals AA_AngelMoth, 1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Races). Phase 0 step P2 (biome_sprint_kickoff_2026-10-15.md 0.5.3), tool src/RimMandrake/Utils/aa_port.py. Free RM_ tier, home mod TheRot.
  Stats, tools, race fields and pawnkind numbers are the donor's own, as the creature the game shows today
  (our rename/tolerance patches on the donor def are folded in). Departures:
    - wildBiomes dropped (the biome roster casts it); AnimalStatExtension (donor stat defs) dropped.
    - VEF.* comps and VEF_ abilities kept, guarded MayRequire OskarPotocki.VanillaFactionsExpanded.Core (a framework we keep, not the donor).
    - texPath is OUR final path; the PNGs are owed through artpipe (no donor art is reused). Until the art is
      installed through the art ledger this def has no picture: ART OWED, never a pass of the art bar.
    - dessicated donor art and alternate random graphics dropped (vanilla fallback).
    - folded 5 op(s) from src/RimMandrake/TheRot/Patches/RotSpecies_NamesAndSizes.xml
    - folded 2 op(s) from src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/AnimalTolerances_Ashkarr.xml
    - folded 3 op(s) from src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/BiomeCastEvictions_WildBiomes.xml
    - leatherDef Leather_Chitin dropped (decoration item; no art owed)
    - customResourceString AA_MothSilkDesc -> 'moth silk' (donor translation key replaced by the words)
    - leatherDef Leather_Chitin dropped (decoration item; no art owed)
    - texPath Things/Item/Resource/AA_EggBeetle -> Things/Item/Resource/RM_DustveilEgg (ART OWED, RM_AngelMothEggFertilized)
    - texPath Things/Item/Resource/AA_EggBeetle -> Things/Item/Resource/RM_DustveilEgg (ART OWED, RM_ButterflyEggUnfertilized)
    - texPath Things/Item/Resource/AA_MothSilk -> Things/Item/Resource/RM_MothSilk (ART OWED, RM_MothSilk)
-->
  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Dustveil</defName>
    <label>dustveil</label>
    <description>A broad-winged moth whose pale, dust-soft wings hang like a veil, bred long ago for some forgotten waste-eating project and long since gone wild. Its grubs are timid things that nibble at sparse growth. The adults are not timid about anything: they eat cloth, wool first and then any natural fibre, worn or stored, and settle for grass only when nothing better is within reach. A tamed one can be shorn of a fine moth-silk, provided the silk is kept well away from every other moth, which will eat that too.</description>
